{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Voices and hail, and fire walking on the earth.</b> It is known that at the time of hail the air changes and illnesses come upon all things composed of the four elements, and the cause of illness in them is the change, corruption, and reversal of the four elements; for so long as they are mingled together and stand according to their balanced disposition, bodies are healthy and strong, and with their reversal illness comes." "<b>And therefore</b> it is possible to interpret that Scripture mentions here the four elements: קולות וברד — voices and hail — are air and water, and ותהלך אש ארצה — 'and fire walking on the earth' — are fire and earth. And it mentions them reversed, to indicate that with the coming of the hail the air changes and the elements reverse from above to below, and the Holy One, blessed be He, does as He wills, to the point that the nature of fire — which is the highest and purest of them all — reverts to the nature of earth, which is the lowest and heaviest of them all. This is what it says: ותהלך אש ארצה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:16.381846245Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}